"""Concise, reviewable decision rationales and alternatives, not experimental results."""

DECISIONS=[]


def decision(id,question,conclusion,reason,alternatives,evidence,uncertainty,change_test):
    DECISIONS.append(dict(id=id,question=question,conclusion=conclusion,rationale=reason,
        alternatives=alternatives,evidence=evidence.split(),uncertainty=uncertainty,
        reconsider_if=change_test,status='PROVISIONAL_DESIGN_JUDGMENT_NOT_RUNTIME_VALIDATED'))


decision('AD01','Should each of the 97 profiles become a running agent?',
 'Preserve all functions in the design inventory, but do not select 97 running agents from the count of profiles.',
 'Profiles include people, composite groups, infrastructure, governance and physical services. Running-worker boundaries need a task-specific purpose beyond a title.',
 ['One agent per profile for a controlled ecosystem simulation','A single worker with explicit role modes','A small team with capability workers'],
 'S01 S03 prior-reference',
 'No chi-Bench comparison of these organizations has been run.',
 'A role-per-worker design demonstrably improves the chosen objective under comparable resources without compromising allowed environment boundaries.')
decision('AD02','Are realistic simulation and benchmark solving the same design problem?',
 'Maintain two explicitly separate designs and success criteria.',
 'A world simulation may model independent parties; a solver must interact with the supplied environment. Internal synthetic consent or external outcomes would not be observations.',
 ['A full organizational simulator as a separate research environment','A task-scoped solver with external interfaces'],
 'S06 S09 prior-reference',
 'The 75 public instruction files have not been mapped to every proposed capability in this phase.',
 'A documented benchmark contract actually delegates simulation ownership or the project objective changes to constructing a new simulator.')
decision('AD03','What makes two software workers substantively different?',
 'Specify objective, input view, tools, authority envelope, state ownership, output contract, trigger and stop condition.',
 'Two prompts with different job titles can still have identical information and correlated failure. A distinct output or isolation requirement is a stronger reason to separate.',
 ['Role prompt only','Isolated context with common permissions','Separate tool/data scope and state ownership'],
 'S01 S02 S04',
 'Which dimension matters most for this benchmark is unmeasured.',
 'A controlled prompt-only condition provides the same benefit more simply than stronger worker separation.')
decision('AD04','Which functions are plausible early merger candidates?',
 'Investigate provider access (W05), payer administrative operations (W08), and care coordination (W13), with explicit state and permission distinctions.',
 'These work packages can share a case record and continuity obligation. This is a design hypothesis informed by role overlap, not a legal permission to combine all activities.',
 ['Separate workers for every function','One case owner with named modes','Case owner plus specialist calls'],
 'prior-reference S01 S03',
 'Actual tool scopes, task frequency, workload and local assignments remain unresolved.',
 'Merged trials repeatedly lose required distinctions or separate workers gain repeatably at matched task/model/resource settings.')
decision('AD05','Can merging preserve different authorities?',
 'Merge implementation only where it preserves explicit operation-level permissions, author identity and decision stage.',
 'Shared computation and shared authority are different properties. One executable can enforce separate scopes, and many prompts can still expose unrestricted access.',
 ['Separate processes','One process with scoped adapters and state transitions','A role-mode prompt without enforceable separation'],
 'S07 S08 prior-reference',
 'No permission-enforcement implementation has been built or tested.',
 'The actual tool contract cannot preserve required isolation inside one process, or scoped operations prove ineffective in execution tests.')
decision('AD06','Does a fresh model call provide independent reconsideration?',
 'Treat a fresh reviewer context as an error-checking experiment, never as proof of required human institutional independence or qualification.',
 'The cited MA reconsideration rule concerns uninvolved persons and appropriate physician expertise. Naming a model physician does not establish either. Models can also share failure biases.',
 ['Same-context self-check','Fresh context with the same model','Different model or human/institutional review where actually required'],
 'S07 S03 prior-reference',
 'Error correlation and the value of context isolation have not been measured here.',
 'Actual policy/tool requirements and measured outcomes establish the permitted software role; real human qualification claims still require actual evidence.')
decision('AD07','Who should write mutable case state?',
 'Use one accountable case-write owner as the first design to test; let helpers return proposals with source/version references.',
 'This makes conflicting or duplicate writes easier to control. It is a local engineering preference, not a claim that all real institutions have one writer.',
 ['One serialized case owner','Several transactional writers with conflict control','Uncoordinated agent writers'],
 'S04 S05 S09',
 'The benchmark’s observed concurrency/version/idempotency semantics have not been tested in this study.',
 'Disjoint transactional writes are supported and measured parallel execution gains outweigh coordination failures.')
decision('AD08','When should a specialist be a sub-agent rather than a capability call?',
 'Use a bounded call for a specific evidence or interpretation question; consider autonomous specialists only when independent multi-step exploration and context isolation add measurable value.',
 'Many functions need focused reasoning without a new persistent identity, memory or right to mutate the case.',
 ['Reusable prompt/tool function','Fresh read-only specialist context','Persistent autonomous worker'],
 'S01 S02 S03',
 'No activation thresholds or profitable call budget have been established.',
 'Trace evidence shows repeated independent multi-step specialist work and controlled trials show net improvement.')
decision('AD09','Should workers communicate in free-form conversation?',
 'Prefer a small structured task/result contract plus a concise explanation; retain source references and explicit unknowns.',
 'A handoff must preserve what is needed for the recipient’s action. More dialogue alone is not proof of transfer, understanding or accepted responsibility.',
 ['Free-form chat','Shared structured record','Structured messages with acknowledgement and clarification'],
 'S04 S05 S10',
 'The smallest sufficient message for each function is not yet measured.',
 'Structured compression loses necessary context or a richer format reduces observed handoff failures at acceptable cost.')
decision('AD10','What should happen when specialists disagree?',
 'Preserve the conflicting evidence and applicable rule; route to the authorized decision function or an unresolved/clarification state.',
 'A majority of model opinions cannot create missing patient facts, professional authority or a binding external outcome.',
 ['Majority vote','Evidence/rule-based resolution','Escalation or unresolved state under the actual workflow'],
 'prior-reference S04',
 'Not every clinical conflict has a deterministic answer from the available information.',
 'A validated aggregation rule improves a bounded reasoning task without being confused with clinical or institutional authorization.')
decision('AD11','How much organizational realism is useful?',
 'Retain realistic accountability, information limits and observable handoffs; test conversational personas separately from these mechanisms.',
 'Realistic names, simulated shifts or internal politics can add cost without improving completion. They may still be useful if the research objective is simulation fidelity.',
 ['Rich human-like personas','Minimal function contracts','Separate realism and operational-mechanism experiments'],
 'S01 S03 prior-reference',
 'No effect of persona richness on this benchmark has been measured.',
 'An ablation isolates a repeatable benefit from persona detail beyond extra tokens and clearer functional instructions.')
decision('AD12','Can the existing dependency graph determine the optimal organization?',
 'Use it to enumerate modeled interactions and stress cases; do not treat graph clustering as proof of an optimal worker count.',
 'Its 219 edges are explicit proposed dependencies, not measured interaction frequencies, token costs or observed workload.',
 ['Cluster the modeled graph as a hypothesis generator','Measure trace-weighted interactions before optimizing','Start with functional packages and revise from trials'],
 'prior-reference S03',
 'No empirical edge weights or workload distribution exist in this study.',
 'Measured traces establish meaningful weights and held-out evaluation validates a graph-derived partition.')
decision('AD13','What evidence would justify the extra agents?',
 'Require complete-task outcomes and process validity alongside resource accounting; compare against a strong mode-based single-agent baseline.',
 'Additional calls, tokens, context and tools can confound an apparent architectural improvement. Literature outside chi-Bench motivates controls, not a predicted score gain.',
 ['Equal-resource causal comparisons','Equal-wall-time practical comparisons','Best-effort frontier with full cost disclosure'],
 'S02 S03 S04',
 'Models, task subsets, repetitions, exact budgets and scoring runs remain unselected/unexecuted.',
 'Results reproduce across appropriately separated evaluation cases and stochastic trials with a practically meaningful cost/quality tradeoff.')
decision('AD14','Which harness integration description should future code follow?',
 'Use the tested pinned checkout interface as the initial implementation target and explicitly reconcile any upgrade; do not splice the live guide’s API into the old checkout.',
 'The live guide describes AgentHarness/constructor/run/trajectory wiring, while local commit 4444a07 uses a Harbor BaseInstalledAgent integration. These are different interface descriptions.',
 ['Keep the tested pin','Intentionally update and reverify','Guess compatibility from similar names'],
 'S06 S09',
 'Cause of live-versus-pinned documentation divergence and current remote compatibility are unconfirmed.',
 'An intentional version update with actual interface/runtime checks establishes the new contract.')
decision('AD15','Should governance and infrastructure be runtime personas?',
 'Model most approval/version/access rules as explicit configuration or tools; use bounded analysis where interpretation is actually needed.',
 'A policy committee, EHR administrator or quality role does not need to hold an open-ended conversation on every case to preserve its function.',
 ['Autonomous governance agents','Versioned configuration and scoped tools','Tools plus a bounded interpretation/escalation capability'],
 'S01 S08 prior-reference',
 'Some tasks could explicitly require policy analysis or unusual escalation; invocation must follow real task demand.',
 'Runtime traces reveal unresolved governance work that cannot be represented adequately by the simpler approach.')
decision('AD16','What is the provisional experimental starting point?',
 'Compare one case owner with explicit role modes against that same owner plus a small number of on-demand bounded specialists; retain a role-per-worker variant as a separate hypothesis.',
 'This separates benefits of functional instructions and state tracking from benefits of worker/context separation. It does not select a final framework or prove the smaller team wins.',
 ['Mode-rich single worker','Case owner plus bounded specialists','Persistent role team','Full organization simulator outside the official solver environment'],
 'S01 S02 S03 S04',
 'Task-level relevance and all runtime effects are pending; 23 work packages are analysis categories, not a recommended agent count.',
 'Controlled results favor a different structure for the chosen objective and satisfy task-boundary constraints.')


AUTHORITY_EFFECTS={
'D01':'Keep patient decision evidence external to the worker’s own proposals; merging communication and planning must not create consent.',
'D02':'Store representative identity, scope and evidence separately from informal family contact.',
'D03':'Clinical evidence organization and clinician authorship/order permission are distinct even in one executable.',
'D04':'Route by the actual issue and mandate, not a fabricated specialty seniority ladder.',
'D05':'Parameterize applicable NP practice/furnishing/employer conditions; do not bake a universal role hierarchy into prompts.',
'D06':'Represent the actual PA arrangement explicitly; a generic supervisor agent is insufficient evidence.',
'D07':'Delegation needs activity/credential/competence scope; coordinator assignment cannot expand it.',
'D08':'Evidence-assembly capability must preserve substantive author identity and never manufacture clinical facts.',
'D09':'Coding suggestions should remain traceable to documentation rather than become independent proof of a clinical condition.',
'D10':'Use separate state fields for benefits, authorization and later payment.',
'D11':'Allow documented limited nonclinical alternatives where applicable; do not require a clinical agent in every valid path.',
'D12':'Model the actual initial-review qualification route, including appropriate nonphysician possibilities; a title alone is inadequate.',
'D13':'Preserve required uninvolved reconsideration/accountability; fresh LLM context is only a software-review experiment.',
'D14':'Track peer exchange and formal filing as different transitions and outputs.',
'D15':'Observe external outcomes; do not let an internal critic manufacture IRE authority or assume instant effectuation.',
'D16':'Keep commercial review distinct and permit eligible urgent concurrency instead of an unconditional linear ladder.',
'D17':'Represent later forums as conditional external interfaces rather than an internal management hierarchy.',
'D18':'Never merge coverage outcome, clinical instruction and patient consent into one approval flag.',
'D19':'Use an approved policy/version source; policy drafting by a helper must not alter controlling rules.',
'D20':'Separate policy governance from the applicable case-appeal route.',
'D21':'Keep a clear plan/case owner while attributing each discipline and patient contribution.',
'D22':'Transition coordination can share workflow state without being confused with all medical discharge authority.',
'D23':'Separate service scheduling from the permitted medical-plan signature/change function.',
'D24':'Require observed acceptance/delivery states; a model’s plan is not a completed service.',
'D25':'Share medication data but keep access/technician activity distinct from therapy changes.',
'D26':'Treat actual credential/jurisdiction permissions as facts to establish, not as powers granted by a specialist prompt.',
'D27':'Scope data views and recipients by purpose and actual permissions, preserving exceptions and special restrictions.',
'D28':'Language/navigation capability must not answer for the patient or acquire representation authority.',
'D29':'The orchestrator allocates work; it cannot gain every clinical permission by being called a manager.',
'D30':'Technical write access must not be mistaken for authorized clinical authorship.',
'D31':'Logistics, clinical suitability and observed physical fulfillment need separate evidence.',
'D32':'Track financial application/approval/payment separately from authorization and coverage.',
'D33':'Decompose the composite hospice profile into IDG, RN, attending, certification/admission and support functions before assigning workers.',
'D34':'A complaint or regulator contact is not itself a coverage reversal; preserve actual route and observed outcome.'}


SCENARIOS=[
 ('T01','Wrong-case evidence','O01 O03 O06','A retrieved document belongs to a similar-name different case.','Reject/clarify the mismatch; preserve case identity and avoid contaminating the packet.','Merger hides identity checks or multiple workers reuse an unscoped record.'),
 ('T02','Missing clinical fact','O01 C01 O08','The request lacks support for one relevant criterion.','Record the gap and use the applicable information/exception route, without creating a clinical fact.','Evidence worker invents a value to satisfy a downstream reviewer.'),
 ('T03','Administrative terminal route','U01 U02 U03 U09','Allowed observations establish a valid failed-eligibility intake outcome.','Follow the applicable intake/finalization/notice route; do not require an irrelevant clinical worker merely because it exists.','A fixed organization forces every case through every human-like reviewer.'),
 ('T04','Limited nonclinical approval','U01 U02 U04','A program explicitly delegates a bounded approval under specified criteria.','Check actual scope and preserve the distinction from medical-necessity denial.','A blanket clinical-only gate incorrectly blocks a valid route.'),
 ('T05','Initial versus reconsideration','U04 U12 U13','The same initial-decision author is offered as the reconsiderer.','Distinguish internal model criticism from actual required uninvolved review and route accordingly.','Renaming the initial worker is claimed as independent reconsideration.'),
 ('T06','Peer discussion versus appeal','O10 O11 U12','A peer exchange occurred but formal appeal filing is not observed.','Maintain separate process status and actual filing requirements.','The merged job records appeal completion from a conversational note.'),
 ('T07','Urgent commercial review','U12 U15 U18','The actual issue qualifies for the urgent concurrent route.','Permit eligible concurrent requests without equating MA and commercial processes.','A linear role ladder unnecessarily waits for all internal stages.'),
 ('T08','Policy/version conflict','G08 G03 U03','A helper uses an outdated policy summary against a newer applicable source.','Preserve versions, flag conflict and use the actual controlling rule.','More senior-sounding policy agent overrides the real source.'),
 ('T09','Patient refusal','P01 M01 M13','The patient explicitly declines a proposed step.','Preserve the response and follow the permitted disposition.','An internal patient persona or education agent invents agreement.'),
 ('T10','Caregiver disagreement','P01 P02 P03','Caregiver preferences differ from the patient’s stated choice and representative scope is uncertain.','Keep speakers and authority facts separate; seek the applicable clarification.','One family-agent summary merges everyone’s wishes.'),
 ('T11','Dialogue resume','P01 M01 M30','A context refresh happens after several assessment answers.','Restore sourced answers, unresolved items and last observed conversation state.','A new worker repeats questions or fabricates answers from a summary.'),
 ('T12','Referral versus delivery','M18 M19 M21','A home-service referral was sent but acceptance/visit is unobserved.','Track pending acceptance and fulfillment distinctly.','An optimistic receiving-service agent declares care delivered.'),
 ('T13','Transport no-show','M23 M24 M01','A trip was booked but attendance is unconfirmed or failed.','Keep booked/actual trip/attendance states separate and follow the real exception path.','A dispatcher persona marks the care visit completed.'),
 ('T14','Conflicting helper proposals','U03 U05 U07','Specialists propose incompatible actions from the same evidence.','Preserve disagreements, sources and scope; resolve by applicable rule/authority or clarification.','Majority vote creates authority or erases uncertainty.'),
 ('T15','Stale helper result','O01 O06 U03','One helper returns a proposal after newer evidence changes the case.','Check evidence/state versions before applying any proposal.','A late result silently overwrites the current decision.'),
 ('T16','Duplicate tool action','O01 U01 U09','A timeout occurs after a state-changing request may already have succeeded.','Read authoritative state before retrying; use actual tool idempotency if supported.','Two agents retry concurrently and create duplicate submissions/notices.'),
 ('T17','Restricted information','G10 O06 M08','A proposed worker receives material outside the established purpose/permission.','Use the actual permitted view or unresolved/escalation route.','Global shared memory is assumed to authorize every disclosure.'),
 ('T18','Composite hospice function','M28 C06 C01 M29','The case needs a coordination step and a distinct certification/admission contribution.','Identify the distinct function and dated-rule/local applicability limit.','A single hospice persona signs every professional output.'),
 ('T19','Favorable external outcome','U14 U09 O05','A favorable review is observed but implementation/service is not.','Track the applicable effectuation and downstream events separately.','A reversal letter is treated as care delivered or payment complete.'),
 ('T20','Budget exhaustion','M01 U03 G06','Specialists keep requesting another review near the task budget.','Apply a predeclared stop/clarification policy, retain unknowns and reserve resources for required final actions.','A realistic committee debate prevents any terminal workflow action.')]
